# Data Agent Database Design

Source of truth for this view: SQLAlchemy ORM metadata under
`backend/libs/basemodel/services_databaseconnector/postgres_orm`.

## Domain Notes

- Tenant boundary: most operational tables hang from `Tenants.id`; RLS depends on
  `tenant_id` plus the runtime `app.tenant_id` setting.
- Knowledge base: `KBData` is the document root; chunks, versions, structured
  import jobs, tables, conflict records, graph and vector metadata fan out from it.
- Agent authoring/runtime: `Agents` owns versions and workflows; conversations
  own messages; messages own traces.
- Semantic layer: `SemanticMetric` is stable identity; `SemanticMetricVersion`
  carries versioned formulas; `SemanticSynonym` maps phrases to metrics.
- Schema discovery: `KBWarehouse` and `SchemaCatalog` describe physical sources;
  they are separate from semantic business definitions.
- Audit/outbox: `AuditLogs`, `DataAccessLog`, and `OutboxEvents` are append-style
  operational records.

